    stages: [{"id":"twist","title":"The twist — 0.97 AUC, useless for early intervention","ask":"Churn model is 0.97 AUC offline but useless for early intervention — a feature encodes the outcome. Find and fix. Minimal scaffold.","attemptHint":"Why does a leaky feature ruin EARLY intervention specifically?","model":"A feature encoding the outcome (e.g. 'cancellation initiated') makes offline AUC near-perfect but fires only once churn is already happening — useless for EARLY intervention, which needs signals available well before the horizon. Enforce point-in-time features aligned to the intervention lead time, drop outcome-encoding features, and re-evaluate at the real decision point.","heuristic":"Leakage that encodes the outcome yields high AUC but no early-warning value; features must precede the intervention window.","control":"Point-in-time features at the intervention lead time; leakage audit.","trap":"Trusting 0.97 AUC that's built on same-time outcome signals.","tell":"The model only 'predicts' churn once it's effectively begun.","anchors":[{"dim":"leak-detected","anchor":"do you find the post-outcome feature (set only after churn intent)?","cost":"0.97 is a mirage; useless for early action"},{"dim":"horizon-honest","anchor":"do you fix features to be as-of an early prediction time?","cost":"you can only 'predict' churn once it's too late to act"},{"dim":"audit","anchor":"do you audit all features for as-of-outcome leakage?","cost":"one leak fixed, others remain"},{"dim":"usefulness","anchor":"can the fixed model predict early enough to intervene?","cost":"a leak-free but too-late model is worthless"}]}],
