    stages: [{"id":"twist","title":"The twist — leetspeak/images/coded evasion","ask":"Your keyword/classifier worked, then abusers used leetspeak, images, and coded language to evade. Make it robust. Scaffold: a classifier exists.","attemptHint":"Surface patterns decay. What's robust to adaptation?","model":"Static surface patterns decay against adaptive abuse. Add signals adversaries can't easily fake — account age, behavioral/graph/coordination signals — alongside multimodal detection (image + text), and retrain continuously on fresh evasions with a fast feedback loop. Robustness comes from hard-to-fake signals and adaptation speed, not a bigger keyword list.","heuristic":"Beat adaptive evasion with hard-to-fake account/behavioral/graph signals + multimodal detection + fast retraining.","control":"Evasion/abuse rate over time; multimodal coverage.","trap":"Extending keyword/rule lists that attackers route around in days.","tell":"Abuse dips after each rule change, then rebounds.","anchors":[{"dim":"evasion-diagnosis","anchor":"do you name adversarial evasion of literal-text detection as the cause?","cost":"you keep patching keywords and lose the race"},{"dim":"hard-to-fake-signals","anchor":"behavioral/account/graph signals adversaries can't easily fake?","cost":"content-only signals are trivially evaded"},{"dim":"multimodal","anchor":"do you cover image/coded content, not just text?","cost":"harm moves to the modality you don't inspect"},{"dim":"retrain-loop","anchor":"retraining on fresh evasion examples + evasion monitoring?","cost":"the model decays as tactics evolve"}]}],
    reference: { type: "solution" }, selfCheck: null,
